From: grenudi <idunerg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-walleye: Enable the ADSP and audio services

Boot the audio DSP from the phone's own firmware (read from its vendor
partition, never shipped), let the seven APR services register without the
protection-domain lookup that Google's firmware never answers, enable the LPASS
SMMU the DSP's buffers need, and describe the MultiMedia frontends, Quaternary
MI2S RX with SD1 only, and its pin groups (labels renamed from porthole's quat_mi2s_active and quat_mi2s_sd1_active, which the overlay stubs already use;
the sound node of the amplifier series uses the new ones).

Taken from porthole's wahoo/taimen dts: the ADSP node and firmware name from
Casey Connolly's 0027, the protection-domain deletes, SMMU, dais and pins from
Giuseppe Maggio's 0084 and 0160. The sound card node is not here: it names the
speaker amplifier of the TAS2557 series.

Co-developed-by: Casey Connolly <casey.connolly@linaro.org>
Signed-off-by: Casey Connolly <casey.connolly@linaro.org>
Co-developed-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: grenudi <idunerg@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-walleye.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-walleye.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-walleye.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-walleye.dts
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@
 
 /dts-v1/;
 
+#include <dt-bindings/sound/qcom,q6dsp-lpass-ports.h>
+
 #include "msm8998.dtsi"
 #include "pm8998.dtsi"
 #include "pmi8998.dtsi"
@@ -476,3 +478,102 @@
 	power-supplies = <&pmi8998_charger>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The audio DSP and its services (item walleye-adsp-q6-mi2s): the ADSP's firmware is the phone's own, read from its vendor partition by the keeper's provisioning;
+ * the APR services (msm8998.dtsi) come up on it. Values after porthole's wahoo/taimen dts (patches 0027, 0084), re-measured nowhere yet.
+ */
+&remoteproc_adsp {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	firmware-name = "qcom/msm8998/wahoo/adsp.mbn";
+};
+
+/*
+ * Google's wahoo adsp firmware does not host the "avs/audio" protection domain (all seven services): the locator answers but never lists it, PDR fails the lookup,
+ * no APR device is registered and the sound card would wait forever. Without the property apr_probe() registers the services directly.
+ */
+&q6core {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
+&q6afe {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
+&q6asm {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
+&q6adm {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
+&q6mvm {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
+&q6cvs {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
+&q6cvp {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
+/*
+ * The audio DSP reaches its PCM buffers only through this SMMU. With it disabled the q6asm dais device gets no IOMMU group, falls back to direct DMA and
+ * hands the DSP a raw physical address (measured above 4 GB on the sister board taimen), which the DSP cannot reach: the SoC dies when the DSP first touches it.
+ */
+&lpass_q6_smmu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+/* MultiMedia1..4, the frontends porthole's board uses. */
+&q6asmdai {
+	dai@0 {
+		reg = <0>;
+	};
+
+	dai@1 {
+		reg = <1>;
+	};
+
+	dai@2 {
+		reg = <2>;
+	};
+
+	dai@3 {
+		reg = <3>;
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * Quaternary MI2S is the only path to the internal speakers: the stereo TAS2557 pair is wired to SD1 with the SoC as bit- and frame-clock master, so only
+ * that data line is claimed and gpio60/SD0 is left alone.
+ */
+&q6afedai {
+	dai@22 {
+		reg = <QUATERNARY_MI2S_RX>;
+		qcom,sd-lines = <1>;
+	};
+};
+
+&tlmm {
+	/* Quaternary MI2S to the TAS2557 amps: SCK/WS on 58/59 (driven high while idle: the amps sample the line), data on 61. The sound card that uses them
+	 * comes with the amp (item walleye-tas2557-driver). */
+	quat_mi2s_pins: quat-mi2s-active {
+		pins = "gpio58", "gpio59";
+		function = "qua_mi2s";
+		drive-strength = <8>;
+		bias-disable;
+		output-high;
+	};
+
+	quat_mi2s_sd1_pins: quat-mi2s-sd1-active {
+		pins = "gpio61";
+		function = "qua_mi2s";
+		drive-strength = <8>;
+		bias-disable;
+	};
+};
